       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose there's a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other harm. The usual starting dose is 25\u201350 mg daily, and the usual range is 50\u2013200 mg daily.\n\nThis may be a typo. For example, 100 mg may have been intended. Orders should also come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient. A non-clinician can't place them, even with the right authority in other areas.\n\n- If a prescriber meant a different dose, such as 50 mg or 100 mg, have them confirm it or enter it themselves. I can enter it once the dose is confirmed.\n- If 1000 mg really is intended, a prescriber and a pharmacist should review it directly first. I'd still need explicit clinical confirmation and a documented rationale.\n\nWhich would you like to do?"
